WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:15.118
In September, Pollyanna started school in Beldingsville.

2
00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:19.701
She quickly made many friends among the boys and girls in her class.

3
00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:24.524
Much to her surprise, she actually enjoyed her schoolwork.

4
00:00:26.046 --> 00:00:29.048
Although she was a happy student, she didn't forget her old friends.

5
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.280
She continued to visit Mrs.

6
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:33.961
Snow and Mr.

7
00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:35.801
Pendleton on a regular basis.

8
00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:42.223
Mr. Pendleton, however, was not happy and complained to her one Saturday afternoon.

9
00:00:42.243 --> 00:00:48.585
"I rarely see you these days," he said as they sat in his library.

10
00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:51.086
"How would you like to come live with me?"

11
00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:54.787
Pollyanna thought he was joking.

12
00:00:54.807 --> 00:00:56.407
"Oh, Mr.

13
00:00:56.487 --> 00:00:58.268
Pendleton, you're so funny!

14
00:00:59.508 --> 00:01:01.770
I thought you didn't like having people in your house."

15
00:01:03.471 --> 00:01:06.093
"That was before you taught me to play your wonderful game.

16
00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:09.235
Now I'm glad to have people here to help me.

17
00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.117
Not that I'll need them forever.

18
00:01:13.237 --> 00:01:15.179
I'll soon be up and walking around as usual.

19
00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:17.520
Then, watch out!"

20
00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:20.742
He playfully shook one of his crutches at her.

21
00:01:22.143 --> 00:01:23.364
Pollyanna frowned at him.

22
00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:28.788
"But you aren't really glad about things; you just say you are.

23
00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:32.354
You know, you never play the game the right way."

24
00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:35.937
Mr. Pendleton looked very serious.

25
00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:40.621
"That's why I want you to live with me—to help me play it.

26
00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:42.442
So will you come?"

27
00:01:42.462 --> 00:01:48.087
"Mr. Pendleton, you don't really mean that."

28
00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:51.229
"Yes, I do."

29
00:01:53.511 --> 00:01:56.614
When Pollyanna realized he was serious, she felt upset.

30
00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:59.156
"You know I can't.

31
00:01:59.528 --> 00:02:00.689
I'm Aunt Polly's!"

32
00:02:02.191 --> 00:02:03.932
He spoke with a sudden fierceness.

33
00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:07.856
"You're no more hers than His voice grew gentler.

34
00:02:07.876 --> 00:02:11.339
"I mean, perhaps she'd allow you to live here.

35
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.601
Would you come, if she let you?"

36
00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:19.687
"But Aunt Polly has been so good to me," Pollyanna said slowly.

37
00:02:19.707 --> 00:02:27.797
"She took me in when I didn't have anybody left but the Ladies' Aid and—" A spasm crossed

38
00:02:27.837 --> 00:02:30.138
Mr. Pendleton's face as if he was in pain.

39
00:02:30.158 --> 00:02:35.061
"Pollyanna, a long time ago, I loved somebody very much.

40
00:02:37.542 --> 00:02:39.543
I had hoped to bring her to this house someday.

41
00:02:40.784 --> 00:02:44.986
I imagined how happy we'd be here and that we'd spend the rest of our lives together."

42
00:02:45.006 --> 00:02:47.667
"Go on."

43
00:02:48.988 --> 00:02:52.490
Pollyanna encouraged him, her eyes full of sympathy.

44
00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:57.821
"But well I didn't bring her here.

45
00:02:59.261 --> 00:02:59.941
Never mind why.

46
00:03:00.442 --> 00:03:01.522
I just didn't, that's all."

47
00:03:03.423 --> 00:03:07.585
Mr. Pendleton gazed out the window for a moment before returning his focus to Pollyanna.

48
00:03:07.605 --> 00:03:14.388
"Ever since then, this great, gray pile of stone has been a house but never a home.

49
00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:19.190
I think it takes a spouse's hand and heart to make a house a home.

50
00:03:20.611 --> 00:03:23.592
Or else a child's presence, and I haven't had that either.

51
00:03:25.044 --> 00:03:29.488
Now that you've heard my story, Pollyanna, won't you come and turn this house into a home?"

52
00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.993
Pollyanna sprang to her feet, her face bright with joy.

53
00:03:35.013 --> 00:03:40.037
"Do you wish you'd had that woman's hand and heart all this time?"

54
00:03:41.818 --> 00:03:42.959
Mr. Pendleton nodded.

55
00:03:42.979 --> 00:03:46.422
"Oh, I'm so glad!"

56
00:03:47.563 --> 00:03:48.864
She sighed contentedly.

57
00:03:48.884 --> 00:03:52.908
"You can take us both, and everything will be all right."

58
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.300
"Take you both?"

59
00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:57.902
Mr. Pendleton was puzzled.

60
00:03:57.922 --> 00:04:02.063
"Well, Aunt Polly isn't persuaded yet.

61
00:04:03.124 --> 00:04:06.845
But I'm sure she will be, if you tell your story the same way you told me.

62
00:04:06.865 --> 00:04:09.927
Then we'll both come live with you!"

63
00:04:11.828 --> 00:04:13.488
A look of terror filled Mr.

64
00:04:13.528 --> 00:04:14.329
Pendleton's eyes.

65
00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:17.350
"Aunt Polly come here?"

66
00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.152
"Unless you'd rather go there?

67
00:04:21.996 --> 00:04:26.780
Her house isn't quite as pretty as yours, but it's—" "Pollyanna, stop!

68
00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.040
What are you talking about?"

69
00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.782
"Where we're going to live, of course."

70
00:04:32.384 --> 00:04:34.805
Surprised by his question, Pollyanna went on.

71
00:04:34.825 --> 00:04:43.812
"You said you wanted Aunt Polly's hand and heart years ago to make a home and—" A cry

72
00:04:43.912 --> 00:04:44.612
came from Mr.

73
00:04:44.652 --> 00:04:46.473
Pendleton's throat.

74
00:04:47.094 --> 00:04:49.816
Before he could speak, the maid suddenly appeared in the doorway.

75
00:04:50.892 --> 00:04:52.834
"Dr. Chilton is here," she announced.

76
00:04:54.655 --> 00:04:55.916
Pollyanna rose to leave.

77
00:04:55.936 --> 00:04:59.718
"Say nothing about what I asked you," Mr.

78
00:04:59.778 --> 00:05:02.400
Pendleton begged Pollyanna in a quiet voice.

79
00:05:03.581 --> 00:05:06.403
Pollyanna broke into a grin and called back over her shoulder.

80
00:05:06.423 --> 00:05:08.124
"Of course not.

81
00:05:08.484 --> 00:05:10.626
I know you'd rather ask Aunt Polly yourself!"

82
00:05:13.007 --> 00:05:17.070
Mr. Pendleton fell back limply in his chair and tried to breathe calmly.

83
00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.412
"What's the matter?"

84
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.702
Dr. Chilton rushed to Mr.

85
00:05:21.762 --> 00:05:24.166
Pendleton's side and felt his racing pulse.

86
00:05:25.989 --> 00:05:27.731
Mr. Pendleton managed a smile.

87
00:05:27.751 --> 00:05:30.495
"Too much of that medicine you prescribed!"
